-- #2074 crossable-set guard: a POLYMORPHIC extern.  No type in FFI-ABI.md
-- section 1 is polymorphic, so a generic foreign declaration is genuinely
-- unrepresentable at a C ABI -- there is no width, no tag, and no marshalling
-- rule to pick.  Inherited from `test/typecheck_fixtures/externs.mdk`'s old
-- `wrapL : a -> List a` cell, which this rule made unacceptable.
--
-- Also the cell for the LOCATION fallback: a bare `TyVar` carries no source loc
-- of its own, so without `ffiCheckExternSig`'s whole-signature fallback the
-- caret for the `a` PARAMETER lands on `:1:0` -- line 1 of a file whose defect
-- is on line 12 -- instead of on this declaration's `Array` head.
extern ffiWrapAll : a -> <FFI> Array a

main : <IO> Unit
main = println "ffi cross poly reject"
